meta {
  name: Dry-run Accesso 1 Crea
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/anncsu/v1/workflows/verifica-e-crea-indirizzo-completo
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-API-KEY: {{apiKey}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "codcom": "H501",
    "denom_odonimo": "DELLE CAVE DEL TRULLO",
    "dug": "VIA",
    "numero_civico": "99999",
    "sezione_censimento": "580911010001"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  // Capture the new progressivi so step 2 suppresses exactly what we created.
  bru.setVar("dryrun_prognaz", res.getBody().progressivo_nazionale_odonimo);
  bru.setVar("dryrun_prognazacc", res.getBody().progressivo_civico);
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

tests {
  test("creation returns 200 with the new progressivi", function() {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.body.progressivo_nazionale_odonimo).to.be.a("string");
    expect(res.body.progressivo_civico).to.be.a("string");
  });
}

docs {
  WRITE OPERATION — step 1 of a self-cancelling "dry-run" pair (mirrors the SDK's
  `anncsu accesso insert --dry-run`, which inserts an accesso and then rolls it back
  with an S operation): create an accesso, then suppress it (step 2) so the overall
  effect on ANNCSU is a no-op. Run only against collaudo (UAT), never production,
  and ALWAYS run "Dry-run Accesso 2 Rimuovi" right after.

  Like the SDK, this targets an EXISTING, uniquely-named odonimo (VIA DELLE CAVE
  DEL TRULLO in H501) so no orphan odonimo is created — only an accesso is added
  then removed. The denomination must be unique in the municipality (ADR 0019) and
  the civic 99999 is chosen to be clearly non-existent, so the create takes the
  insert branch (not an update of a real civic) with no collision.

  The post-response script stores the returned progressivi
  (progressivo_nazionale_odonimo, progressivo_civico) in collection variables that
  step 2 reads — run the two in sequence (or run the whole collection in order).

  Note: ANNCSU suppression is a dated LOGICAL suppression, so step 2 leaves a
  suppressed record rather than erasing all trace — there is no true delete.
}
